---
description: Default agent posture — scope, approvals, communication
alwaysApply: true
---

# Agent core

- Follow the user’s request only. No drive-by refactors, unrelated files, or extra docs.
- Prefer absolute paths; run commands yourself; don’t ask the user to run what you can run.
- Never update git config. Commit / push / PR only when explicitly asked.
- Never install new npm packages without explicit approval. Use only `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (never bare `pnpm i` / `pnpm install`).
- Before changing any address, token, Discord link, or https URL: double-check; do not “fix up” links.
- Communicate briefly. Lead with the answer. Bold sparingly. No engagement baiting.
- If a task needs a plan with real trade-offs, say so once — then execute after the user chooses (or when the choice is obvious from prior rules).
